# Generated Gazebo worlds: rebuilt from the committed OSM snapshot on demand.
simulation/worlds/generated/

# Raw gz capture streams a scenario writes while it flies and deletes on the way
# out. A run that is killed never reaches that cleanup, and these reach gigabytes
# -- one interrupted matrix left 3.6 GB behind and a commit that GitHub refused.
# They are working files, never evidence: the evidence is the JSON report.
simulation/artifacts/**/.*-scans.jsonl
simulation/artifacts/**/.*-pose.jsonl

# Per-mission raw telemetry sample streams. One 10-run P0.v2 matrix writes 168 MB
# of these, and the five retained 2026-07-21 matrices came to 547 MB between them
# -- against 6.6 MB for everything else those same runs produced. The verdict a
# gate turns on lives in the p0-*.json report and the mission artifacts, both of
# which stay committed; this is the sample-by-sample record behind them. Dropping
# it costs the ability to re-derive a run's telemetry offline, which is a real
# loss and the reason this is a deliberate trade rather than cleanup.
simulation/artifacts/**/telemetry-history/

# Atomic-write temporaries. A writer renames these into place, so one only
# survives a crash mid-write; two were tracked by accident in fcf317e.
simulation/artifacts/**/*.tmp

# Local tool output, not project state.
.coverage
graphify-out/
.codex/environments/
